    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.basics\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHi echasnovski! Is it possible to add options to disable default plugins loaded in vim like and more if any of them are missing in the list.\r\n```\r\n                \"2html_plugin\",\r\n                \"tohtml\",\r\n                \"getscript\",\r\n                \"getscriptPlugin\",\r\n                \"gzip\",\r\n                \"logipat\",\r\n                \"netrw\",\r\n                \"netrwPlugin\",\r\n                \"netrwSettings\",\r\n                \"netrwFileHandlers\",\r\n                \"matchit\",\r\n                \"tar\",\r\n                \"tarPlugin\",\r\n                \"rrhelper\",\r\n                \"spellfile_plugin\",\r\n                \"vimball\",\r\n                \"vimballPlugin\",\r\n                \"zip\",\r\n                \"zipPlugin\",\r\n                \"tutor\",\r\n                \"rplugin\",\r\n                \"syntax\",\r\n                \"synmenu\",\r\n                \"optwin\",\r\n                \"compiler\",\r\n                \"bugreport\",\r\n```\r\nAlso it would be really helpful if the default plugins which are not used much like tutor, zip, etc which are not used much be disabled by default.",
